# AEP core rules

This repository is the **Agentic Engineering Platform** reference instance. Follow the configured organization, not generic agent defaults.

## Authority (read first)

- @CLAUDE.md — agent working agreement, validate-before-push, branching (POL-001)
- @.agentic/project.yaml — runtime preferences, human gates, work store
- @.agentic/hooks/hooks.yaml — when checks must run (Cursor hooks in @.cursor/hooks.json are the IDE adapter)
- @docs/DOCUMENTATION_INDEX.md — corpus reading order
- @docs/policies/POL-001-BRANCHING-AND-MERGING.md — branch naming, squash merge, trailers

## Non-negotiables

1. **Human at the top.** Never set `human_approved: true` or close a gate without an approval record under `.agentic/approvals/` (ADR-019).
2. **One work store.** Work state lives only in `.agentic/work/`. No `TODO.md`, no checkbox task lists in docs.
3. **Role ≠ model.** Role files under `.agentic/roles/` never name a provider or model; resolve runtime from `project.yaml` `runtime_preferences`.
4. **Agents never merge.** `engineer.primary` denies `github.merge`; open PRs, humans merge (ISC-30).
5. **Validate before push.** Run `python3 scripts/validate_docs.py`, `python3 scripts/check_gates.py --strict --base origin/main`, and `go test ./...` when `cmd/` or `internal/` change.

## Branching

Per POL-001: `<type>/<work-item-number>-<kebab-summary>` (e.g. `feat/50-ba-loop`). Squash merge only; `Closes WI-NNNN` in the commit message.
